  "cards": [
    {
      "title": "Two Independent Type Axes",
      "dot": "cyan",
      "items": [
        "KDA/DSA selects attention; dense/MoE selects FFN. A KDA layer can use MoE, so KDA does not mean dense.",
        "Router correction bias affects expert selection; combine weights use normalized original sigmoid scores.",
        "The shared expert does not compete in the 8-of-288 selection. Kernels may fuse it, but both mathematical contributions remain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Activation and Width",
      "dot": "amber",
      "items": [
        "Dense, routed, and shared paths use clamped SwiGLU: gate capped at 10, up clipped to [−10,10], then SiLU(gate) times up.",
        "Widths are complete logical widths. TP partitions and EP dispatch do not add network layers."
      ]
    }
  ]
